# Agoge Wrestling Academy

MERN-stack marketing/info website for a wrestling gym. Customers visit to view
info (programs, schedule, staff, pricing) and enroll. Enrollment links out to an
external registration platform (placeholder links for now).

## Design reference

The layout replicates `Beebe/beebetrained-source.html` (extracted from the
client-provided view-source file `Beebe/view-source_beebetrained.com.html`) with
Agoge branding and a black/gold/red Spartan color scheme. See the
`design-system` rule for the palette.

## Structure

- `frontend/` — Vite + React 19 (JSX) single-page site. Builds to `frontend/build/`.
  - `src/data/siteContent.js` — default content object + `deriveContent()` helper.
    Live content is fetched from `/api/content` at runtime (see below).
  - `src/data/ContentContext.jsx` — `ContentProvider` fetches `/api/content` and
    merges over the bundled defaults; components read via `useContent()`.
  - `src/components/` — one component per page section, each with a co-located `.css` file.
  - `src/admin/` — the `/admin` content editor (login + per-section forms).
  - `src/index.css` — theme variables, buttons, shared section styles, forms.
- `backend/` — Express 5. Content API is live (no DB): `GET /api/content` (public),
  `PUT /api/content` (JWT-protected), `POST /api/admin/login`. Content persists to
  `backend/data/content.json` (gitignored; seeded from `content.default.json`).
  Contact/review routes still return 501; contact form uses mailto and reviews
  use localStorage until wired.
- `deploy/` — `deploy.ps1` (build + upload script) and `nginx-agoge.conf` (server config).
- `Beebe/` — reference source from the site the client wants replicated. Do not modify.
  Excluded from git (root `.gitignore`) — local only.

## Admin content editor (/admin)

Navigating to `/admin` renders `frontend/src/admin/AdminApp.jsx` (branch in
`main.jsx`, no router). Login is a single admin password: bcrypt hash in the
backend `.env` (`ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH`, generate with
`node backend/scripts/hash-password.js "pw"`) plus `JWT_SECRET`; login returns a
12h JWT kept in sessionStorage. Saves replace the whole content JSON (validated
top-level keys, 200KB cap, atomic write). Editing content requires NO rebuild —
the public site fetches it at runtime. Both env vars must be set on the droplet
or admin login returns 503.

Coach portraits are optional `image` fields on staff objects. The Staff editor
uploads JPG/PNG/WebP files (5MB max) through `POST /api/admin/coach-images`;
the backend normalizes them to 640x800 WebP files in
`backend/data/uploads/coaches/` and serves them from `/api/uploads/`. Runtime
uploads are gitignored and excluded from deploy archives so production images
survive deployments. Staff cards display these portraits as full-card
backgrounds beneath a dark overlay, with a Lambda watermark fallback.

## Current placeholder status

Business content (address, phone, email, coach names, stats, schedule,
registration URLs, Instagram, logo) is ALL placeholder — defaults live in
`backend/data/content.default.json` and `frontend/src/data/siteContent.js`
(keep the two in the same shape). The logo is a temporary Λ text mark until
the client provides a real one.

